  "description": "There's more to good mulled apple cider than swirling in a couple sticks of cinnamon.",
  "notes": "Optional or for serving: Optional additions (see notes): 1 tablespoon brandy, raw sugar, lemon zest; Extra brandy, lemon slices, and/or freshly grated nutmeg, for serving (optional)\n\nNotes: Ciders can vary greatly in sweetness and acidity. Adjust the final seasoning of the mulled cider with a spoonful of alcohol to enhance the fruity aromas, raw sugar to bring out the spice, and/or lemon to balance the sweetness. We recommend cider-friendly liquors, such as brandy, bourbon, or dark rum.",
